TITLE:: FoaVHAP
summary:: B-Format Virtual Hemispherical Amplitude Panning Transform
categories:: UGens>Ambisonic
related:: Classes/FoaEncode, Classes/FoaDecode, Classes/FoaRTT

DESCRIPTION::
FoaVHAP is a B-format ambisonic transform that synthesizes or enhances the height channel (Z) using Virtual Hemispherical Amplitude Panning (VHAP). It reconstructs plausible height information from the horizontal components (W, X, Y) and optionally blends it with the existing Z channel.

The transform is particularly useful for:
- Enhancing B-format signals derived from UHJ (where Z was discarded)
- Adding perceptually plausible height to horizontal-only recordings
- Creating vintage-style height enhancement effects

The processing uses FIR convolution with psychoacoustically-designed kernels that inject quadrature band-passed height components, primarily in the 900-4000Hz and 4000-12000Hz ranges.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
Main audio rate processing method.

ARGUMENT:: input
A 4-element array containing B-format components [W, X, Y, Z].

ARGUMENT:: trim
Height synthesis level trim in dB (-12.0 to +12.0, default 0).
Allows matching the synthesized Z' level to the original Z level.

ARGUMENT:: morph
Morph amount between original and synthesized Z (0.0 to 1.0, default 1).
- 0.0 = original Z only
- 1.0 = full blend with synthesized Z'
- Values between create a controlled blend

ARGUMENT:: solo
Solo mode for auditioning (0 or 1, default 0).
- 0 = normal mode (W/X/Y passthrough, processed Z output)
- 1 = solo mode (synthesized Z' routed to W and Z channels for monitoring)

ARGUMENT:: partitionSize
FIR partition size for convolution (256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096, or 8192, default 1024).
Larger sizes are more efficient but have higher latency.

returns:: A 4-element array of processed B-format signals [W, X, Y, Z].

METHOD:: balanced
Convenience method with balanced preset configuration.

ARGUMENT:: input
A 4-element array containing B-format components [W, X, Y, Z].

ARGUMENT:: trim
Height synthesis level trim in dB (-12.0 to +12.0, default 0).

ARGUMENT:: morph
Morph amount (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.8 for balanced enhancement).

returns:: A 4-element array of processed B-format signals with balanced settings.

METHOD:: cleanup
Cleans up global kernel buffers. Call this when done using FoaVHAP to free memory.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// Basic VHAP enhancement
(
{
    var input, enhanced;
    
    // Create test B-format signal (horizontal plane only)
    input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),  // W
        SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,  // X (front-back)
        SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,  // Y (left-right)
        0  // Z (no height)
    ];
    
    // Apply VHAP enhancement
    enhanced = FoaVHAP.ar(input, trim: 0, morph: 0.8);
    
    enhanced;
}.play;
)

// Solo mode for auditioning synthesized height
(
{
    var input, solo;
    
    input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.1),
        SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1,
        SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1,
        0
    ];
    
    // Solo the synthesized Z' component
    solo = FoaVHAP.ar(input, trim: 3, morph: 1, solo: 1);
    
    solo;
}.play;
)

// Integration with ATK encoding/decoding chain
(
{
    var stereo, encoded, enhanced, decoded;
    
    // Start with stereo source
    stereo = [SinOsc.ar([440, 880]) * 0.1].flatten;
    
    // Encode to B-format using UHJ
    encoded = FoaEncode.ar(stereo, FoaEncoderKernel.newUHJ);
    
    // Apply VHAP enhancement
    enhanced = FoaVHAP.balanced(encoded, trim: 0);
    
    // Decode to binaural
    decoded = FoaDecode.ar(enhanced, FoaDecoderKernel.newListen(1053));
    
    decoded;
}.play;
)

// Parameter control
(
var synth = {
    var input, output;
    
    input = [
        WhiteNoise.ar(0.05),
        SinOsc.ar(\freq.kr(440)) * 0.05,
        SinOsc.ar(\freq.kr(880)) * 0.05,
        0
    ];
    
    output = FoaVHAP.ar(
        input, 
        trim: \trim.kr(0),
        morph: \morph.kr(0.8),
        solo: \solo.kr(0)
    );
    
    output;
}.play;

// Control parameters
synth.set(\trim, 3);     // Boost synthesized height
synth.set(\morph, 1.0);  // Full blend
synth.set(\solo, 1);     // Solo mode
synth.set(\solo, 0);     // Back to normal
)

// Clean up when done
FoaVHAP.cleanup;
::
